  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Where is your family from?",
     "texto": [
      "**Quê chị ở đâu?** = Where are you from? (literally «where is your home village?»). «quê» is your family's home, even if you live in another city. It's one of the first things you'll be asked.",
      "**Tôi sinh ra ở …** = I was born in… · **Tôi sinh ra tại một làng nhỏ.** = I was born in a small village (tại = in, more formal than ở).",
      "To speak respectfully about someone who has died, you say **mất**: **Ông tôi đã mất.** = My grandfather passed away. The opposite: **Bà tôi còn sống.** = My grandmother is still alive.",
      "In the family: **con cả** = the eldest son; **con út** = the youngest."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "North, centre and south",
     "texto": [
      "Vietnam is divided into three regions: **miền Bắc** (the north, with Hà Nội), **miền Trung** (the centre, with Huế and Đà Nẵng) and **miền Nam** (the south, with Thành phố Hồ Chí Minh).",
      "The compass points: **Bắc** (north), **Nam** (south), **Đông** (east), **Tây** (west). For north-east and south-west the order is the other way round from English: **Đông Nam** = south-east, **Tây Bắc** = north-west.",
      "In the south of the country is the Mekong delta: **đồng bằng sông Cửu Long**. In the north, the Red River delta: **đồng bằng sông Hồng**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
